# Code style and templates

2 spaces, no tabs, across Nunjucks/HTML/JS/Sass/JSON.

- Complex logic belongs in `routes.js`, not the view — keep templates simple.
- One question per page.
- Match existing patterns in the codebase before introducing a new style.
- Use includes for repeated content. Keep `data['field-name']` access consistent with the rest of the codebase.
- Class order: component → modifier → width/sizing → spacing → display, e.g. `govuk-input govuk-input--error govuk-!-width-one-half govuk-!-margin-bottom-4`.

Use the Prototype Kit's built-in templates (**Manage your prototype → Templates**) for standard page types.

```nunjucks
{% extends "layouts/v4.html" %}
{% set version = "v4" %}
{% set pageName = "Change company name" %}
{% set activeSection = "providers" %}
{% block beforeContent %}
  {{ govukBackLink({ text: "Back", href: "/" + version + "/software-providers/" + provider.id }) }}
{% endblock %}
{% block content %}
  <div class="govuk-grid-row">
    <div class="govuk-grid-column-two-thirds"><!-- content --></div>
  </div>
{% endblock %}
```

Links to pages that don't exist yet go to the version's `placeholder.html` page (see the project folder structure rule), not a dead link or a stubbed-out real page.
